{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795529892,"nonce":"V6B5I/WR7ETpnB6ocK34tBvZYVI=","message":"Empty Metal command buffers: a wgpu-hal experiment, not committed.\n\nwgpu-core 26 records each pass into its own hal command buffer and inserts a transition buffer before it (CommandEncoder::close_and_swap). wgpu-hal 26.0.5's Metal begin_encoding makes an MTLCommandBuffer at once, and Metal's transition_buffers/transition_textures encode nothing, so every pass costs an empty command buffer: created, committed and completed. The submission table of the Metal trace showed 15 submitted command buffers per slide frame at d9b3db91, 8 of them with an encoder.\n\nExperiment: a copy of wgpu-hal 26.0.5 (outside the cargo registry) whose Metal encoder makes the MTLCommandBuffer on the first command that needs it; end_encoding hands back None when nothing was encoded and submit skips it; the fence signal goes on the last non-empty buffer or a new one as before. Wired through a temporary [patch.crates-io], reverted after.\n\n- Submitted command buffers per frame: slide 15 -\u003e 9, structural 36 -\u003e 16.\n- Scripted swipe (period 14, 80 swipes), /usr/bin/time -l interleaved: about 23.6e9 instructions (23.94, 23.18, 23.61) -\u003e about 21.9e9 (21.78, 21.96, 22.05), 7% less; user+sys 4.8 s -\u003e 4.2 s mean.\n- With the patch: blinc_gpu + blinc_app --run-ignored all 767 of 768 (tbc canary), blinc_recorder headless --run-ignored all 385 of 385.\n\nCarrying it needs a decision: a vendored or forked wgpu-hal under [patch.crates-io] (workspace builds only; crates.io users of blinc_gpu would not get it), or a change upstream. The diff:\n\n```diff\ndiff -ru wgpu-hal-26.0.5/src/metal/command.rs wgpu-hal/src/metal/command.rs\n--- wgpu-hal-26.0.5/src/metal/command.rs\t2006-07-24 02:21:28\n+++ wgpu-hal/src/metal/command.rs\t2026-11-24 14:07:46\n@@ -33,10 +33,32 @@\n }\n \n impl super::CommandEncoder {\n+    /// The command buffer being encoded, made on first use.\n+    fn cmd_buf(\u0026mut self) -\u003e metal::CommandBuffer {\n+        if self.raw_cmd_buf.is_none() {\n+            let label = self.pending_label.take().flatten();\n+            let queue = \u0026self.raw_queue.lock();\n+            let retain_references = self.shared.settings.retain_command_buffer_references;\n+            let raw = objc::rc::autoreleasepool(move || {\n+                let cmd_buf_ref = if retain_references {\n+                    queue.new_command_buffer()\n+                } else {\n+                    queue.new_command_buffer_with_unretained_references()\n+                };\n+                if let Some(label) = label {\n+                    cmd_buf_ref.set_label(\u0026label);\n+                }\n+                cmd_buf_ref.to_owned()\n+            });\n+            self.raw_cmd_buf = Some(raw);\n+        }\n+        self.raw_cmd_buf.as_ref().unwrap().to_owned()\n+    }\n+\n     fn enter_blit(\u0026mut self) -\u003e \u0026metal::BlitCommandEncoderRef {\n         if self.state.blit.is_none() {\n             debug_assert!(self.state.render.is_none() \u0026\u0026 self.state.compute.is_none());\n-            let cmd_buf = self.raw_cmd_buf.as_ref().unwrap();\n+            let cmd_buf = self.cmd_buf();\n \n             // Take care of pending timer queries.\n             // If we can't use `sample_counters_in_buffer` we have to create a dummy blit encoder!\n@@ -191,22 +213,8 @@\n     type A = super::Api;\n \n     unsafe fn begin_encoding(\u0026mut self, label: crate::Label) -\u003e Result\u003c(), crate::DeviceError\u003e {\n-        let queue = \u0026self.raw_queue.lock();\n-        let retain_references = self.shared.settings.retain_command_buffer_references;\n-        let raw = objc::rc::autoreleasepool(move || {\n-            let cmd_buf_ref = if retain_references {\n-                queue.new_command_buffer()\n-            } else {\n-                queue.new_command_buffer_with_unreta